From 5abae9d1b5457f2c812384f1f485e3f6d3c0da52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Levine <blahm1d@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 5 Jul 2026 11:07:28 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] core: P0011 - MMTM register-list mask is reversed vs
 MMFM

MMTM and MMFM use opposite bit->register mappings (MMFM: bit N = R(N);
MMTM: bit N = R(15-N)), verified against MAME's 34010ops.hxx and unidasm
on real Smash T.V. code (matching push/pop pairs carry bit-reversed list
words, e.g. MMTM 0x8b00 / MMFM 0x00d1 = {A0,A4,A6,A7}). birdybro mapped
both identically (A0026), which passes its same-word round-trip TB but
corrupts registers on real code that pushes/pops the same regs with
different (reversed) words.

Fix: unify the mm iterator to highest-set-bit-first for both; add
mm_reg_idx = is_mmtm ? 15-mm_iter_idx : mm_iter_idx to drive the MMTM
push read port. MMFM unchanged.

This was the boot derail: the string routine at ffea8df0 pushed the
mirror-image register set, so the ffea8f70 MMFM popped a code address
(0xFFEA57B0) into A0 -> ffea9090 JRLS fell through where MAME takes it
-> illegal opcode at fff0a78a (cyc 1745583). Post-fix A0 is correct,
JRLS matches MAME, boot runs with no derail through 6M cycles.

Also updates the MMTM/MMFM unit TBs to the correct reversed encoding and
adds a reset-vector init (mem[510]=mem[511]=0) so P0001's reset-vector
read starts them at word 0 (pre-existing harness breakage, unrelated to
P0011). tb_mmtm / tb_mmfm / tb_mmtm_nflag all PASS.

